# Line endings are a property of this repository, not of the machine that
# happens to check it out. Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` — which
# ships in the SYSTEM gitconfig of Git for Windows — gives a Windows worktree
# CRLF while the index stays LF. That is not cosmetic here: it breaks
# byte-exact fixture comparisons in tests/i18n-pipeline.test.ts, and it makes
# `node benchmark/make-tabstat-seed.mjs --check` report a seed drift that never
# happened — a false alarm indistinguishable from real corruption of the
# benchmark instrument.
#
# The index is already fully LF, so this file changes only what lands in
# working trees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Files where CRLF is actively dangerous, stated explicitly ------------
# A shell script or a git hook read by a POSIX shell must be LF. Git for
# Windows' bundled MSYS bash tolerates CRLF; /bin/sh on Linux and in the
# worker image does not.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
.husky/pre-commit text eol=lf
.husky/_/*      text eol=lf

# --- Binaries: never transformed, never diffed as text -------------------
# .glb are the viz 3D models (13 tracked); text=auto's binary heuristic would
# almost certainly get these right, but "almost" is not a contract for an
# asset that fails silently when mangled.
*.glb    binary
*.png    binary
*.webp   binary
*.ico    binary
*.gz     binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.pdf    binary

# .svg is XML — keep it text so it diffs and normalises like source.
*.svg    text eol=lf
